Pseudo-BNF
----------

package     = header, file*

file        = pathLength, path, dataLength, data

header      = 'P', 'K', 'G', version, packageSize
version     = UBYTE      # Must be 1
packageSize = LONG      # total package size in bytes, including header

pathLength  = LONG
path        = BYTE[pathLength+1] # NUL-terminated pathname field
dataLength  = LONG
data        = BYTE[dataLength]

All LONG fields are unsigned 32-bit big-endian values.

The canonical writer rounds the stored path field up to a multiple of four
bytes with NUL padding. pathLength is the stored field size minus one. The
pathname value ends at the first NUL byte; any remaining bytes in the field
are padding.

Example
-------

"PKG", 1, 28L, 3L, "foo", 0, 8L, "barbarba"
